Kreative Studio pose editor (STU-PE1). Plain JavaScript, no libraries, no build step. The same file runs in Node 22 (CommonJS require) and in the browser (classic <script>, no modules). Use exactly this wrapper and nothing outside it:

(function () {
  'use strict';
  const NS = typeof module === 'object' && module.exports ? null : (globalThis.KKPose = globalThis.KKPose || {});
  const need = (name, file) => (NS ? NS[name] : require(file));
  // ... the code; get other pose modules with need('vec', './vec.js') INSIDE functions (load order in the browser is free) ...
  const api = { /* exported names */ };
  if (NS) NS.<NAME> = api; else module.exports = api;
})();

Angles are degrees in every API. Coordinates are metres: +X is the figure's left, -Y its front, +Z up. Matrices are arrays of 9 numbers, row-major. Do not change the test file.


Write public/js/pose/project.js (NAME = project): the camera of the pose renders and the OpenPose keypoints. Use need('vec','./vec.js') and need('skeleton','./skeleton.js') inside the functions (V, S). w below is the result of fk.solve(pose): {pos: {name: [x,y,z]}, rot: {...}}.

Export:
- makeView(opts, w): opts = {yaw = 0, pitch = 0, width = 512, height = 768, pad = 0.06, scale, center}. R = V.matMul(V.axisAngle([1,0,0], pitch), V.axisAngle([0,0,1], yaw)). View space v = R * p: v[0] goes to the image right, v[2] up, v[1] away from the camera.
  When opts.scale and opts.center are both given: s = opts.scale, c = V.matVec(R, opts.center).
  Else fit every point of w.pos: rotate each with R, take minX/maxX of v[0] and minZ/maxZ of v[2]; s = Math.min(width * (1 - 2*pad) / (maxX - minX), height * (1 - 2*pad) / (maxZ - minZ)); c = [(minX + maxX) / 2, 0, (minZ + maxZ) / 2].
  Return {R, s, c, width, height, scale: s, center: V.matVec(V.transpose(R), c)}.
- toScreen(view, p): v = R*p; return [width/2 + s*(v[0] - c[0]), height/2 - s*(v[2] - c[2]), -s*(v[1] - c[1])] (the third number is depth, bigger = nearer the camera).
- fromScreen(view, x, y, z): the inverse: v = [(x - width/2)/s + c[0], c[1] - z/s, (height/2 - y)/s + c[2]]; return V.matVec(V.transpose(R), v).
- keypoints(view, w): returns {width, height, body, left, right}. body = S.BODY18 mapped to points, left = S.HAND mapped with 'l_' + name (S.HAND[0] is 'wrist', so 'l_wrist'), right with 'r_'. A point is [x, y] = the first two numbers of toScreen rounded to 0.1 (Math.round(x*10)/10), or null when x < 0, y < 0, x >= width or y >= height. Face points (nose, l_eye, r_eye, l_ear, r_ear) are also null when turned away: d = V.matVec(R, V.sub(w.pos[name], w.pos.head)); l = Math.hypot(d[0], d[1]); null when l > 0 && -d[1] / l < -0.2.
- openposeJSON(kp): {canvas_width: kp.width, canvas_height: kp.height, people: [{pose_keypoints_2d, hand_left_keypoints_2d, hand_right_keypoints_2d, face_keypoints_2d: []}]} where each list is flat [x, y, 1] per point of kp.body / kp.left / kp.right, and [0, 0, 0] for a null point.
